assistant_message.content:
First, find the total amount of rice Goldy bought.

\[
\text{Number of sacks}=20,\qquad 
\text{Weight per sack}=25\text{ kg}
\]

\[
\text{Total weight}=20 \times 25 = 500\text{ kg}
\]

Goldy paid **18 000 pesos** for all the rice, so the price per kilogram is

\[
\text{Price per kg}= \frac{\text{Total cost}}{\text{Total weight}}
                    = \frac{18\,000\text{ pesos}}{500\text{ kg}}
                    = 36\text{ pesos/kg}
\]

\[
\boxed{36\text{ pesos per kilogram}}
\]
